@@ -58,6 +58,20 @@ In addition, the `md_globals` parameter of
 `Markdown.extensions.Extension.extendMarkdown()` is no longer recognized as a
 valid parameter and will raise an error if provided.
 
+### `UnescapePostprocessor` replaced with `UnescapeTreeprocessor`
+
+Backslash escaped characters are now restored by the new
+`markdown.treeprocessors.UnescapeTreeprocessor` (registered as `unescape` with
+a priority of `0`) before the tree is serialized, rather than by
+`markdown.postprocessors.UnescapePostprocessor` after serialization. This
+ensures that escaped characters which are special to HTML (such as `\"` in an
+attribute value when the [smarty](../extensions/smarty.md) extension is
+enabled) are properly escaped in the output. As a side effect, `\>` is now
+output as `&gt;` rather than `>`.
+
+The `UnescapePostprocessor` is no longer registered by default. It is
+deprecated and raises a `DeprecationWarning` when instantiated.
+
 ## New features
 
 The following new features have been included in the 3.4 release:
@@ -97,3 +111,5 @@ The following bug fixes are included in the 3.4 release:
 
 * Extension entry-points are only loaded if needed (#1216).
 * Added additional checks to the `<pre><code>` handling of `PrettifyTreeprocessor` (#1261, #1263).
+* Backslash escaped characters no longer result in invalid HTML in attribute
+  values (e.g. `![x\"x](x)` with the smarty extension).
